[01:46.92]reputation [ˌrepjuˈteɪʃn]n. 名气，名声；名誉 搭 have a reputation for 以…而闻名 / live up to one's reputation 名副其实
[01:57.24]perpetuate [pəˈpetʃueɪt]vt. 使永久；使长存 例 These measures will perpetuate the influence of the brand.
[02:07.32]exert [ɪɡˈzɜːt]vt. 努力；运用；施加；行使 例 The manager exerts a lot of pressure on the development division to deliver the hot patch for the client. 搭 exert oneself to do sth. 努力做某事 / exert pressure on sb. 对某人施加压力 / exert sb.'s utmost 尽某人最大的努力
[02:30.48]earnings [ˈɜːnɪŋz]n. 挣得的财物；工资；利润
[02:34.08]morale [məˈrɑːl]n. 士气，斗志；道德；风纪 例 A couple of victories can improve the team's morale greatly.
[02:43.68]prospect [ˈprɒspekt]n. [常pl.] 机会，前途；期望；景色； 将要发生的事；可能成为主顾(或应征者)的人；有 希望的候选人 例 The general manager is confronted with the prospect of bankruptcy of his own company. 搭 in prospect of 可期待；在望，有希望
[03:03.36]lure [lʊə(r)]vt. 吸引；引诱，诱惑 n. 吸引力；诱惑 物；诱饵，鱼饵 例 If you can't withstand the lure of benefits, please quit now! 搭 lure sb. into a trap 引诱某人中圈套
[03:17.04]frustrate [frʌˈstreɪt]vt. 使沮丧，使灰心；挫败，使受挫 折；阻止，妨碍 vi. 受挫，失败；灰心，丧气 例 Delight and satisfy your visitors with smart design decisions rather than frustrating and annoying them.
[03:35.04]overland [ˈəʊvəlænd]a. 经由陆路的；陆上的 ad. 陆上； 通过陆路
