[04:04.20]nurture [ˈnɜːtʃə(r)]vt. 养育，培养；鼓励 n. 养育，培养 例 Parents have taken painstaking care to nurture and raise their child.
[04:15.84]aspiration [ˌæspəˈreɪʃn]n. 热望，渴望；期望 例 This reafflrms the unequivocal position and sincere aspiration of the Chinese government. 搭 have no aspiration 不图成名 / have soaring aspiration 有雄心壮志
